# Names only. Never put real values in this file; real values go in .env.local (git-ignored)
# and in Vercel/Supabase environment settings.
#
# Safe for the browser (public by design; access is enforced by RLS):
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# The project this app may talk to; the app refuses any other (a stray production .env cannot be used by accident):
# RIO_SUPABASE_ALLOWED_REF=<20-character ref of the project, or "local" for a local stack>
#
# Server only. Never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_ and never commit.
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=<server-only secret key; bypasses RLS, used only by trusted server code>
# Cloudflare R2 (private bucket, no public domain). Put the real values in .env.local, never in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ name:
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID=<32-character Cloudflare account id>
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<R2 API token access key id, scoped to the one bucket>
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=<R2 API token secret access key>
# R2_BUCKET_NAME=<bucket name, lowercase letters, digits and hyphens>
# Master switch for JUDGE PLAYBACK (M5). Server-only. ONLY the exact value "yes" lets the server sign a short-lived (5 minute) link to an
# assigned judge's entry; anything else means OFF, in the page, the action and the dependency builder. Needs the secret key and R2
# settings above and migration 00700. Keep it "no" until a real playback test is approved:
# RIO_PLAYBACK_ENABLED=no# Judge invitations from /admin/judges. Server-only. OFF unless the value is exactly "yes"; until then the form is disabled, says so, and no Supabase Auth
# call is made. Turn it on only after Supabase Authentication has working custom SMTP, the "Invite user" template from supabase/templates/invite-judge.html is
# pasted in, Site URL is set, and a test invitation has been received. Needs SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY (never NEXT_PUBLIC). The invitation e-mail is sent by Supabase
# Auth itself; this app never sends, sees or stores a password.
# RIO_STAFF_INVITES_ENABLED=no
# Manual judge accounts from /admin/judges (Add judge, Reset password). Server-only. OFF unless the value is exactly "yes"; a different switch from the invitations one, which
# it never reads. An administrator creates the account directly (no e-mail is sent): the server generates a strong password, shows it once, and the judge must choose their
# own at first sign-in. Needs SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY (never NEXT_PUBLIC). Changing it needs a redeploy.
# RIO_STAFF_PROVISIONING_ENABLED=no
##
# Length of the email one-time code. Server-only, optional; unset means 6, allowed 6 to 10.
# It must equal the OTP length of the Supabase project this environment talks to (Authentication, Providers, Email).
# Set it per environment (.env.local for dev, Vercel settings for production). A wrong value stops sign-in; it never guesses.
# RIO_OTP_LENGTH=6
#
# Express API (server-side only; the browser never calls it directly). Defaults shown; set them only if yours differ:
# RIO_API_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:4000
# This site's own origin, sent to the API on state-changing requests; it must be listed in the API's ALLOWED_ORIGINS:
# RIO_ADMIN_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3001
